// fixture-457: BUG-root-authority-kdl-transitive.md case D.
//
// Same shape as fixture-456 (case B), but root pins "softlink" via an
// `overrides {}` rule (the spec-blessed remedy per §10.1) instead of a
// direct root dep declaration — the OTHER form the bug report shows
// collapsing resolution identically. "proptest" (a fetched dep) declares
// "nim-z3" and "softlink" as git deps in its OWN milpa.kdl; the override
// targets the exact same source (URL+ref) proptest's OWN claim on
// "softlink" uses.
//
// Pre RFC origin-as-identity, the override-seeded provenance_gate entry
// still collapsed the same way as case B: "nim-z3" — declared in
// proptest's kdl and NOT overridden by anyone — lost its entire candidate
// set as collateral damage (the bug report's "sibling package losing
// candidates when a claim is suppressed" symptom).
//
// Expected (post RFC origin-as-identity S3a/S3b BindingResolver): resolves
// cleanly — "proptest", "softlink" (via the override target), and "nim-z3"
// all present, with no collateral candidate loss.
name "t"
kind "application"
deps {
    "proptest" git=(url)"https://example.com/proptest.git" ref="main"
}
overrides {
    pkg "softlink" git=(url)"https://example.com/softlink.git" ref="main"
}
